      "message": "This does an RPC to PackageManager to query packages, which may be a bit heavy, even though it shouldn\u0027t be necessary in most cases; also it\u0027s not very clear why that\u0027s generally necessary.\n\nYou could do that only if it\u0027s U-, and the caller has REGISTER_NSD_OFFLOAD_ENGINE permission, e.g.:\n\n```\n// REGISTER_NSD_OFFLOAD_ENGINE was only added to the SDK in V, but may\n// be backported to older builds: accept it as long as it\u0027s signature-protected\nif (PermissionUtils.checkAnyPermissionOf(REGISTER_NSD_OFFLOAD_ENGINE)\n    \u0026\u0026 (isAtLeastV() || PermissionUtils.isSystemSignaturePermission(...))) {\n    return;\n}\n\nPermissionUtils.enforceNetworkStackPermissionOr(context, NETWORK_SETTINGS);\n```\n\nThis won\u0027t be called often so it doesn\u0027t matter that much, but it makes it clearer when this check is actually necessary",
